            'note' => 'Core point has $\\ge MinPts$ within $\\epsilon$-radius; Border point has $< MinPts$ but falls within $\\epsilon$-radius of a core point; Noise point is neither. Discovers arbitrary non-spherical cluster shapes and naturally isolates noise outliers without pre-specifying K.',
