        [
            'text' => 'Why is Apache Parquet the industry-standard file format for analytical data lakes? Explain how columnar storage, snappy/gzip compression, dictionary encoding, and file metadata statistics (min/max per row group) allow query engines to perform predicate pushdown and column projection.',
